EF AI Workspace (#167): artifacts that work with the live model. Owner request 2026-10-24: "do full QA in artifacts,
make it work very well because not works yet; also make the chat smart, generate artifact when they need it".

- Artifacts mode from the spec (utils/endpoints.ts, hooks/Agents/useApplyModelSpecAgents.ts): the specs run in the
  `custom` mode, with their own Arabic artifact instructions (librechat.yaml). A mode stored by the former switch is
  ignored, so LibreChat's English artifact prompt (which says to prefer in-line content) never comes back.
- No «مستندات» switch (Chat/Input/Artifacts.tsx removed, BadgeRow.tsx, ToolsDropdown.tsx): artifacts are always on, as
  in Claude; the instructions decide when to create one.
- The model's own form (Artifact.tsx): Qwen writes the document straight inside `:::artifact` without the fenced
  block, or fences it with fewer backticks than its own code blocks use. The panel received the words run together;
  the container's source is now taken from the message, without its outer fence.
- Local preview (StaticArtifactFrame.tsx, ArtifactPreview.tsx, ArtifactFixButton.tsx, utils/artifactTab.ts):
  documents, pages, drawings and code show in a srcdoc frame sandboxed without allow-same-origin (an opaque origin),
  built from the same page Sandpack served (Tailwind, the EF font), instead of a round trip to codesandbox.io's static
  server. The page's own errors reach Try fixing; the panel's refresh reloads it. React keeps Sandpack.
- Tests: MarkdownBlocks.artifactSource.test.tsx (both renderers); applyModelSpecEphemeralAgent.test.ts follows the
  spec-owned mode.

